  "timeframe": "Current state; for jobs, review the most recent ~30 days",
  "criteria": "Check for: notebook instances with direct internet access enabled or root access enabled; missing KMS encryption on notebook volumes, endpoints, training/processing job volumes and output; training jobs/models/endpoints without VPC config or without network isolation or inter-container traffic encryption; Studio domains using public internet access (AppNetworkAccessType PublicInternetOnly) or lacking KMS; overly permissive SageMaker execution roles (e.g. AdministratorAccess, s3:* on *, iam:PassRole on *); publicly accessible or unencrypted S3 buckets used for SageMaker artifacts if easily identified; endpoints with data capture to unencrypted locations; old/unsupported notebook platform identifiers; missing tags/lifecycle configs only if notable. Return a concise summary: counts of resources reviewed, then findings with severity, resource names, and a one-line remediation each. Note anything you could not check due to permissions."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Assess SageMaker security posture in us-east-1"}, {"id": "tooluse_TvqbuyJOJ8uK2X9wjlev4t", "tool_name": "subagent", "input": {"name": "createtrainingjob-denial-lookup", "agent_type": "generic", "preloaded_skills": ["investigating-infrastructure-changes"], "prompt": "{
  "task": "Find the denied sagemaker:CreateTrainingJob call(s) from yesterday and explain exactly why they were denied.",
  "context": "The user says their user's sagemaker:CreateTrainingJob call was denied yesterday. The user's identity wasn't specified, so find all AccessDenied/UnauthorizedOperation CreateTrainingJob events for IAM users in the window and report each distinct principal. Use CloudTrail (via the CloudTrail lookup tool), then read-only IAM calls (get/list/simulate) to explain the denial. Do not make any mutating calls.",
  "resources": ["sagemaker:CreateTrainingJob", "region us-east-1 (also check other regions if none found there)", "account 012345678901_1"],
  "timeframe": "2026-11-13T00:00:00Z to 2026-11-14T00:00:00Z (widen by a few hours on each side to account for local timezone)",
  "criteria": "From the CloudTrail event, extract time, principal ARN, source IP, errorCode and errorMessage. Determine the denial type: implicit deny (no allow), explicit deny in an identity policy, permissions boundary, SCP, resource-based or session policy, a missing iam:PassRole on the training role, a condition-key failure (e.g. VPC config required, KMS key, tag, source IP, MFA), or a service quota/validation error mistaken for a denial. Identify the specific policy/statement responsible if possible (e.g. via the decoded authorization message or iam simulate-principal-policy), and state the minimal fix. Be clear about what is confirmed vs. inferred."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Find why CreateTrainingJob was denied yesterday"}], "created_at": null}

